  "Question": "Let\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} S_n&=1-2+3-4+\\cdots\\\\ &\\quad+(-1)^{n-1}n. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nHere \\(n=1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(\\ldots.\\) Then \\(S_{17}+S_{33}+S_{50}\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(2\\)",
    "D": "\\(-1\\)",
    "E": "\\(-2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each positive odd-numbered term and the following negative even-numbered term have sum \\(-1\\):\n\\[\n1-2=-1,\\qquad 3-4=-1,\\qquad\\ldots.\n\\]\nThere are eight such pairs in \\(S_{17}\\), followed by \\(+17\\), so \\(S_{17}=-8+17=9\\). Similarly, \\(S_{33}\\) has sixteen pairs followed by \\(+33\\), giving \\(S_{33}=-16+33=17\\). All fifty terms of \\(S_{50}\\) form twenty-five pairs, so \\(S_{50}=-25\\).\n\nTherefore,\n\\[\nS_{17}+S_{33}+S_{50}=9+17-25=1.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{1}\\), choice B.",
